# Machine-readable single source of truth for the Doris baseline this repo's
# BE patch (doris-patches/) applies against. Read by tools/doris-baseline.sh
# and referenced by PATCHES.md. Format: KEY=VALUE, '#' comments, blank lines ok.
#
# Bump procedure + re-vendor log live in PATCHES.md (§Re-vendor log).

# UPSTREAMED: the fe-connector catalog SPI merged into apache/doris `master` (#64304 + the whole
# fe/fe-connector tree). The pre-merge brikk fork `branch-catalog-spi` is RETIRED — we now vendor
# straight from apache/doris master. master keeps the SHA alive itself, so there is no fork-mirror
# baseline branch to maintain.
PIN_SHA=ded91fb9fb30e9192a7d14387e63fda973f57293

# Upstream commit subject at the pin (match by subject if the SHA is ever GC'd on origin).
PIN_SUBJECT=[fix](ci) Skip usage-limited Codex review accounts (#66319)

# Author/commit date of the pinned commit (informational).
PIN_DATE=2026-08-01

# Upstream remote. Clone/fetch this at PIN_SHA. (Was the brikk/doris fork mirror while the SPI lived
# on the pre-merge branch-catalog-spi line; now it is apache/doris master.)
FORK_URL=git@github.com:apache/doris.git

# Branch the tool clones before checking out PIN_SHA. RELABELED from the retired dated fork-mirror
# branch to plain `master` now that the SPI is upstreamed (tools/doris-baseline.sh clones
# --branch "$FORK_BRANCH" then detaches at PIN_SHA). Simplest local path: skip the clone by pointing
# DORIS_SRC at the existing apache checkout (DORIS_SRC=~/DEV/OSS/doris).
FORK_BRANCH=master

# The upstream line this baseline tracks (informational; do not build a blind tip — pin PIN_SHA).
UPSTREAM_BRANCH=master

# OPERATING MODEL: local-only, no fork push. The BE patch is applied against a local apache/doris
# master checkout at PIN_SHA (the worktree ~/DEV/OSS/doris); SPI jars are built from that checkout's
# fe/ into the project-local doris-duckbridge/doris-m2/. The FE is patch-free (SPI upstreamed).
# FORK_BRANCH is retired — master, not a dated fork mirror, keeps PIN_SHA alive now.
